🚀 Execution Steps
Step 1: Clone Repository & Update Username
Update <your-dockerhub-username> in deployment.yaml and commands.sh with your actual Docker Hub username.

Step 2: Build & Push Docker Image
Bash
docker login
docker build -t <your-dockerhub-username>/nginx-pod-ip:v1 .
docker push <your-dockerhub-username>/nginx-pod-ip:v1
Step 3: Deploy to Kubernetes
Bash
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
kubectl apply -f service.yaml
🧪 Testing Load Balancing
Execute curl multiple times to verify traffic distribution across different Pod IPs:

Bash
curl http://localhost:30080
Output:

HTML
<h1>Container / Pod IP: 10.244.0.5</h1>
(Subsequent requests will cycle through 10.244.0.6, 10.244.0.7, etc.)

🧹 Cleanup
Bash
kubectl delete -f deployment.yaml
kubectl delete -f service.yaml
